 proprietary brands, such as FOSSIL, SKAGEN, MICHELE, RELIC, and ZODIAC; and under the licensed brands, including ARMANI EXCHANGE, DIESEL, EMPORIO ARMANI, KATE SPADE NEW YORK, MICHAEL KORS, SKECHERS, and TORY BURCH. It sells its products through company-owned retail and outlet stores, department and specialty retail stores, mass market stores, e-commerce sites, licensed and franchised FOSSIL retail stores, retail concessions, and airlines, as well as operate stores under the WATCH STATION and WSI brands. The company was formerly known as Fossil, Inc. and changed its name to Fossil Group, Inc. in May 2013. Fossil Group, Inc. was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Richardson, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Franco  Fogliato | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $223K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Stock-based compensation of $515 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Fossil Group, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $499M market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -16% over the past three years and -11% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -9% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $60M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 69/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"3 Intriguing Stocks to Buy After Q3 Earnings Beats: FOSL, FLY, NYAX","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/commentary/3029019/3-intriguing-stocks-to-buy-after-q3-earnings-beats-fosl-fly-nyax?cid=CS-ZC-FT-investment_ideas-302901